<p>Hello <%= @user.first_name %>,</p>

<p>
  The following side letter obligations need your attention.
  Overdue items are listed first.
</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th align="left">Status</th>
      <th align="left">Investor</th>
      <th align="left">Obligation</th>
      <th align="left">Clause</th>
      <th align="left">Due Date</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @items.each do |item| %>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <% case item["kind"] %>
          <% when "overdue" %>
            <strong style="color: #b02a37;">Overdue</strong>
          <% when "due" %>
            <strong style="color: #cc8a00;">Due today</strong>
          <% else %>
            Upcoming
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <td><%= item["investor_name"] %></td>
        <td><%= item["title"] %></td>
        <td><%= item["source_clause"] %></td>
        <td><%= item["due_date"] %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>
  Completing the linked task records the fulfillment against the obligation.
  You can review the full obligation matrix from the Side Letter Obligations agent page.
</p>

<p>Regards,<br/><%= @entity.name %></p>
